WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.350
A seemingly throwaway line from Avengers:
Endgame got some comic fans' attention, as

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.680
it just may have teased the arrival of a classic
Marvel hero for phase 4 of the MCU.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.720
Or, on the other hand...maybe it hasn't.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.710
Such is the state of studies at Marvel Cinematic
University, better known as MCU, of course.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.080
Be advised that major spoilers for Endgame
follow.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.660
During his mission to secure more Pym Particles
at the SHIELD Base in 1970, Steve Rogers finds

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.960
himself in the office of director Peggy Carter.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.860
He's taken aback by his proximity to his long-lost
flame and the picture of him lovingly displayed

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.440
on her desk, and let's be honest, so was the
audience.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.680
It's a poignant, heartstring-tugging moment,
so it's pretty easy to miss what Peggy seems

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.680
to be saying as Rogers gazes at her through
the office window.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.210
According to one intrepid Reddit poster who
claims to have seen the flick with a closed

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.230
captioning device, Carter says: "Braddock
hasn't checked in.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.340
I'm not a meteorologist and it's not lightning."

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.380
Now, we haven't been able to directly confirm
that this is the dialogue she speaks.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.670
And you probably know to take the average
Reddit post with a grain of salt in terms

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.520
of its overall reliability.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.840
Additionally, Carter delivers the dialogue
while she's in another room, so the line itself

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.940
is pretty hard to hear without the aid of
a closed captioning device.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.150
But if the post is accurate and Carter does
mention "Braddock," it could very well be

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:14.900
referring to a classic Marvel character who
has yet to show up in the MCU: Brian Braddock,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.300
better known as the superpowered Captain Britain.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:23.000
Making his first appearance in Captain Britain
#1 in 1976, Brian Braddock was a graduate

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.840
of London's Thames University, working as
a physicist on an experiment involving antimatter

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.960
particles under Dr. Hugo Travis.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.399
When a villain descended on the facility to
steal the research, Braddock fled to get help,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.220
but crashed his motorcycle and sustained what
would have been fatal injuries — and that's

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.260
when his story took a turn for the weird.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.889
On the verge of death, Braddock was discovered
by none other than Merlin, the legendary wizard

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:45.860
of English folklore.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:50.640
Sensing Braddock's heroic heart, Merlin gave
him a choice of two objects: the Sword of

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.240
Might, or the Amulet of Right.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.330
Not believing himself to have the heart of
a warrior, Braddock chose the amulet — and

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:00.859
upon receiving it, he was transformed into
Captain Britain, with his own snazzy costume

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:05.720
and a bunch of superpowers like super-strength,
super-endurance, and flight, among others.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.980
Captain Britain isn't the only prominent hero
named "Bradock" in Marvel Comics lore — the

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.060
other is his twin sister, Betsy Braddock,
who eventually became the superhero known

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:14.900
as Psylocke.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.099
She showed up in 20th Century Fox's X-Men:
Apocalypse in 2016, played by Olivia Munn.

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:23.930
But Captain Britain does seem like a more
likely candidate for a future appearance in

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.640
the MCU for a few reasons.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.040
For starters, Psylocke's own comic book origin
story is even more bonkers than the one we

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.640
just described for Captain Britain.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.920
Not only that, but Psylocke's status as a
member of the X-Men cast of characters means

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.530
it's pretty unlikely she or any of the other
Marvel Mutants will show up in the MCU too

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.560
soon, since Disney's acquisition of 20th Century
Fox is still so fresh.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.040
More importantly, however, is the fact that
Marvel Studios boss Kevin Feige has actually

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.280
admitted that he and his colleagues have discussed
bringing Captain Britain into the MCU.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.320
In 2017, during the press tour for Spider-Man:
Homecoming, Feige was asked about the potential

00:02:58.329 --> 00:03:00.860
status of a cinematic version of Captain Britain:

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.600
"We have discussed it, we have discussed it,
there are a lot of actors that come in and

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.160
ask about that, about that part.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:07.900
So we'll have to see."

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.459
Could this be the first hint that Captain
Britain is coming?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.520
Could there be yet another Captain being added
to the MCU?

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.300
Or is this all just one wild goose chase based
on a misheard line of dialogue?

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.920
When it comes to the Marvel Cinematic Universe,
all things are possible.

